{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfZueraM3XtxS8piY6NRk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## ANALYSIS Findings\n\n**Requirement, restated:**\nAdd a POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint that cancels active orders by changing status to CANCELLED, cancels all CREATED shipments, and prevents creating shipments for cancelled orders.\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- Order entity: `Order.kt:11-16` — no status field yet\n- OrderController: `OrderController.kt:15-46` — handles POST/GET\n- OrderRepository: `OrderRepository.kt:10-27` — in-memory ConcurrentHashMap\n- Shipment entity: `Shipment.kt:9-27` — already has ShipmentStatus (CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED)\n- ShipmentController: `ShipmentController.kt:20-56` — handles POST/GET\n- ShipmentRepository: `ShipmentRepository.kt:10-27` — in-memory ConcurrentHashMap\n- Error handling: `ApiExceptions.kt` and `ApiError.kt` — ConflictException (409), ResourceNotFoundException (404), ErrorCode enum\n\n**Conventions this repository already has:**\n1. Errors thrown as ApiException subclasses (ConflictException, ResourceNotFoundException) with ErrorCode and message\n2. GlobalExceptionHandler centralizes error response formatting into ApiError envelope\n3. All error scenarios have distinct ErrorCode enum values (ORDER_NOT_FOUND, ORDER_ALREADY_EXISTS, SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS)\n4. In-memory repositories use ConcurrentHashMap, no transactions needed\n5. Tests check both HTTP status and error body structure ($.error.code, $.error.message)\n6. Shipments already support multiple statuses; Order will need OrderStatus enum\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `Order.kt` — add `status: OrderStatus` field and enum\n2. `OrderController.kt` — add cancel endpoint, inject ShipmentRepository to query shipments by orderId\n3. `ShipmentRepository.kt` — add `findByOrderId(orderId: String)` method\n4. `ShipmentController.kt` — check order status before creating shipment\n5. `ApiError.kt` — add error codes for cancel scenarios\n6. `OrderControllerTest.kt` — add tests for cancel endpoint\n7. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — add test verifying shipment creation fails for cancelled orders\n\n**Risks:**\n- Concurrency: multiple cancel requests on same order. Mitigated by repository design (ConcurrentHashMap is atomic for save, but read-modify-write is not). Will need to be careful about ordering.\n- Breaking change: adding status field to Order. Existing tests must still pass; need to verify JsonPath can find the field or use default.\n- Missing shipment query: need way to find all shipments for an order.\n\n**Open questions:**\nNone that change correct behaviour. Error codes (e.g., ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT) are not specified but pattern is clear from existing API.\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **Order.kt**: Add `enum class OrderStatus { ACTIVE, CANCELLED }` and field `status: OrderStatus` to Order data class. New orders default to ACTIVE.\n\n2. **OrderController.kt**: \n   - Inject InMemoryShipmentRepository \n   - Update POST /orders to set status=ACTIVE when creating\n   - Add POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint:\n     - Fetch order; throw 404 if not found\n     - If status==CANCELLED, return 200 with order (idempotent)\n     - If any shipment has status==CONFIRMED, throw 409 with new error code\n     - Otherwise: set order.status=CANCELLED, save order, update all CREATED shipments to CANCELLED, return order\n\n3. **ShipmentRepository.kt**: Add `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` to query shipments for an order.\n\n4. **ShipmentController.kt**: \n   - Inject InMemoryOrderRepository\n   - In POST /shipments create endpoint, after validating shipmentId uniqueness, fetch order\n   - If order doesn't exist, create shipment anyway (keep current behaviour per ticket)\n   - If order exists and status==CANCELLED, throw 409 with new error code\n   - Otherwise, create shipment normally\n\n5. **ApiError.kt**: Add error codes:\n   - `ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT` — cancel blocked by confirmed shipment\n   - `ORDER_IS_CANCELLED` — shipment creation blocked by cancelled order\n\n6. **OrderControllerTest.kt**: Add tests for:\n   - Cancel active order returns 200 and order has status CANCELLED\n   - Cancelling already-cancelled order returns 200 and succeeds (idempotent)\n   - Cancel with confirmed shipment returns 409 and nothing changes\n   - Cancel non-existent order returns 404\n\n7. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt**: Add test for:\n   - Creating shipment for cancelled order returns 409 with error code\n\n**Alternative rejected:**\n- Alternative: Use `findAll()` to query shipments. Rejected because inefficient and error-prone for large datasets. Better to have explicit method.\n- Alternative: Have cancel endpoint also fetch order from database. Rejected because repository.findById() is synchronous and in-memory, so this is same cost anyway.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\nCase 1: Cancel ACTIVE order with all CREATED shipments\n- Read Order from repo\n- Read all Shipments via findByOrderId\n- Check no CONFIRMED shipments exist\n- Update Order status to CANCELLED, save\n- Update each CREATED Shipment status to CANCELLED, save\n- Return 200 with updated Order\n\nCase 2: Cancel already-CANCELLED order\n- Read Order from repo, see status==CANCELLED\n- Return 200 with Order (idempotent, no changes)\n\nCase 3: Cancel order with CONFIRMED shipment\n- Read Order, read all Shipments\n- Find at least one CONFIRMED\n- Throw ConflictException(ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT)\n- Return 409, nothing saved\n\nCase 4: Cancel non-existent order\n- Read Order, get null\n- Throw ResourceNotFoundException(ORDER_NOT_FOUND)\n- Return 404\n\nCase 5: Create shipment for CANCELLED order\n- Validate shipment ID uniqueness\n- Fetch Order\n- If Order exists and status==CANCELLED, throw ConflictException(ORDER_IS_CANCELLED)\n- Return 409, nothing saved\n\nCase 6: Create shipment for non-existent order\n- Validate shipment ID uniqueness\n- Fetch Order, get null\n- Continue with creation (current behavior preserved)\n- Return 201\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\nOrderControllerTest:\n- `cancels_active_order_and_updates_status()` — create order, cancel, verify response has status CANCELLED, verify persisted\n- `canceling_already_cancelled_order_succeeds()` — cancel twice, verify both succeed\n- `cancel_fails_with_409_if_shipment_confirmed()` — create order & shipment, confirm it (direct repo write), cancel, verify 409 and error code, verify order still ACTIVE\n- `cancel_nonexistent_order_returns_404()` — cancel unknown order, verify 404 with ORDER_NOT_FOUND\n\nShipmentControllerTest:\n- `creating_shipment_for_cancelled_order_fails_with_409()` — create order, cancel it, try to create shipment, verify 409 with ORDER_IS_CANCELLED\n- (plus ensure we still handle non-existent order correctly)\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2121,"cache_read_input_tokens":20114,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2121},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0acaa7a7-b8d6-4736-a7af-cbcd6ee22e27","uuid":"f890f280-2914-44e1-ade1-1a23c233ed16","timestamp":"2026-09-30T16:05:14.253Z","request_id":"req_011CfZuerE1Z2KNr84zdHGws"}
